      <comment>interwiki</comment>
      <text xml:space="preserve">''See also:''
[[1873 in music]],
[[1874|other events of 1874]],
[[1875 in music]] and the
[[list of 'years in music']].

== Events ==
*[[Richard Wagner]] moves into the villa at [[Bayreuth]].

== Classical music ==
* [[Anton Bruckner]] - ''[[Symphony No. 4 (Bruckner)|Symphony No. 4]]''
* [[Antonín Dvořák]] - ''String Quartet No. 7 opus 16 in A minor''
* [[Friedrich Kiel]] - ''Christus'' (oratorio)
* [[Edouard Lalo]] - ''[[Symphonie Espagnole]] opus 21 in D minor''
* [[Modest Petrovich Mussorgsky]] - ''[[Pictures at an Exhibition]]'' (for piano)
* [[Pyotr Ilyich Tchaikovsky]] - ''[[Piano Concerto No. 1 (Tchaikovsky)|Piano Concerto No. 1]]''

== Opera ==
* [[Johann Strauss II]] - ''[[Die Fledermaus]]''

== Published popular music ==
* &quot;Crimson Roses In the Heather&quot; by [[Caroline Dana Howe]] &amp; [[William Howard Doane]]
* &quot;Laughing Eyes Of Blue&quot; w. J. Cheever Goodwin m. [[Edward E. Rice]].  Performed by [[Eliza Weathersby]] in the burlesque musical ''[[Evangeline]]''
* &quot;Oh! Dat Watermelon!&quot; by [[Luke Schoolcraft]]

==[[Musical theater]]==
* ''[[Evangeline]]'' a US burlesque musical based upon a poem by Longfellow opened at [[Niblo's Gardens]] on [[July 27]] and ran for only 16 performances before moving to [[Boston]].
* ''[[Whittington]]'', London production

== Births ==
* [[January 4]] - [[Josef Suk (composer)|Josef Suk]] - [[Czech Republic|Czech]] composer and violinist (d. 1935)
* [[January 29]] - [[Charles E. King]], US composer and singer
* [[February 20]] - [[Mary Garden]], Operatic soprano
* [[March 31]] - [[Henri Marteau]], [[France|French]] composer and violinist
* [[July 26]] - [[Serge Koussevitzky]], [[Russia]]n-born conductor and double-bassist
* [[September 13]] - [[Arnold Schoenberg]], composer
* [[September 21]] - [[Gustav Holst]], [[England|English]] composer
* [[October 20]] - [[Charles Ives]], [[United States|American]] composer (d. 1954)
* [[November 12]] - [[Bert Williams]]
* [[December 13]] - [[Josef Lhévinne]], [[Russia]]n pianist
* [[December 22]] - [[Franz Schmidt]], [[Austria]]n composer (d. 1939)
* [[December 25]] - [[Lina Cavalieri]], glamourous opera singer (d. [[1944]])

== Deaths ==
* [[March 20]] - [[Hans Christian Lumbye]], [[Denmark|Danish]] composer and conductor (b. 1810) ([http://www.beethovenfm.cl/cgi-bin/enciclopedia_persona.cgi?id=159], [http://www.danbbs.dk/~erikoest/hclyear.htm])
* [[October 26]] - [[Peter Cornelius]], [[Germany|German]] composer (b. 1824)

[[Category:1874|Music]]
