        <ip>86.134.144.159</ip>
      </contributor>
      <text xml:space="preserve">'''Dodmen''' are the [[human]]-shaped [[geoglyph]]s of [[Britain]], designed in the likeness of their creators.  These creators were the [[surveyor]]s and [[astronomer]]s of the pre-[[Druidry|druid]]ic [[British Isles]].

Dodmen are often mentioned in the context of [[ley line]] theories.

It is also the old Norfolk word for &quot;snails&quot; (Singular - Dodman).

{{UK-hist-stub}}
{{archaeology-stub}}
[[Category:Pseudoarchaeology]]
[[Category:Geoglyphs]]</text>
