      <text xml:space="preserve">{{Not verified}}
'''Mudug''' is a region (''gobolka'') in central [[Somalia]]. Its capital is [[Galcaio]]. It is bordered by [[Ethiopia]], the Somalian regions of [[Nugaal]] and [[Galguduud]] and the [[Indian Ocean]]. 

Mudug is home to several rival [[clan]]s. The majority of the population belongs to either the [[Leelkase]] or [[Habr Gidr|Habargidir]] clans. There are several other clans in Mudug, including the [[Majeerteen]], [[Marehan]], [[Awrtable]], [[Carab Saalax]], and [[Dir (clan)|Dir]]. There is also a considerable amount of [[Midgaan]] in Mudug. Somali [[Bantu]]s were virtually unknown to the region prior to the civil war. 

== Districts ==
Mudug Region consists of five districts: 
*[[Gaalkacyo]]
*[[Galdogob]]
*[[Hobyo]]
*[[Jariban]]
*[[Haradhere]]

===Villages between Gaalkacyo and Goldogob===
*[[Bayra]]
*[[Roox]]
*[[Bur Saalax]]
*[[Laanmadoow]]
*[[Rigoomane]]
*[[Bashka]]
*[[Daresalaam]]
*[[Qansaxle]]
*[[Isqambuus]]

{{Somalia_Regions}}

{{AfricaE-geo-stub}}

