      <text xml:space="preserve">'''Jubbada Dhexe''' is a region (''gobolka'') in southern [[Somalia]]. Its capital is [[Bu'aale]]. It is bordered by [[Kenya]], the Somalian regions of [[Gedo]], [[Bay, Somalia|Bay]], [[Shabeellaha Hoose]] and [[Jubbada Hoose]] and the [[Indian Ocean]].
Until in the mid 1980's with  the exception of Bu'alle and Gilib districts, the whole of the region espcially the part that borders with Kenya was part of the Upper Juba region of Somalia with Baidoa being its capital.

It is roughly the same size as Awdal and Gedo regions in Somalia. [[Banaadir]] region ([[Mogadishu]])is the smallest regions in Somalia. 
It consists of the following districts:
*Bu'aale (capital)
*El Waq (Ceel Waaq)
*Sakow
*Dujuma
*Jilib (Gilib)
 

{{Somalia_Regions}}

{{AfricaE-geo-stub}}</text>
