  <page>
    <title>Detached binary</title>
    <id>185170</id>
    <revision>
      <id>32530011</id>
      <timestamp>2005-12-23T22:20:17Z</timestamp>
      <contributor>
        <username>Jyril</username>
        <id>39573</id>
      </contributor>
      <minor />
      <comment>[[WP:AWB|Assisted]] stub sorting</comment>
      <text xml:space="preserve">'''Detached binaries''' are a kind of [[binary star]]s where each component is within its [[Roche lobe]]. The stars have no major effect on each other, and essentially evolve separately. Most binaries belong to this class, like for example, [[Sirius]].

[[Category:Binary stars]]

{{star-stub}}</text>
    </revision>
  </page>
