      <text xml:space="preserve">[[Image:Latex weapons.jpg|thumb|100px|right|A latex [[Sword]] and [[Dagger]]]]
'''Latex weapons''' are facsimile [[weapon]]s made of [[latex]], and are the primary weapons used in [[live action role-playing game]]s.  Used in [[Europe]] since about 1987, latex weapons are now also in use in the [[United States|US]] LARPing community.

Latex Weapons basically consist of:
* core made of [[Glass-reinforced plastic|fiberglass]] rod ([[Graphite-reinforced plastic|carbon fiber]] is a superior, but more expensive substitute and for short weapons [[Polyvinyl chloride|PVC]] electric tubing is a cheaper alternative)
* Foam (usually in three layers of about half an inch each)
* A few layers of [[latex]]
* Paintwork and design
* A [[silicone]] coating to make the weapon less sticky

== External links ==
* [http://home.clara.net/arianrhod/Aldebaran/DoItYourself/index.html The DIY Guide to LRP] - a do-it-yourself construction guide
* [http://www.elbenschmie.de/ Elbenschmiede] - sample galleries and weapons with detailed photos can 

{{rpg-stub}}
{{weapon-stub}}

[[Category:Live-action role-playing games]]

[[de:Polsterwaffen]]</text>
    </revision>
